      "value": "[auto-routed: surprise=1.00] Implement the family function for the rigid linear constraint family (linear function f(x)=ax+b) to provide a provable low-dimensional, unique solution space. This will serve as a \"zero-violation anchor\" (Step 0) to validate that the experimental setup can achieve zero-violation with sufficient width, before scanning N_c(w). The linear family ensures the optimization landscape is convex and free of local minima traps, isolating whether any observed flatness in N_c(w) for other families is an optimization artifact or a property of the constraint space itself."
